---
description: Commit messages, no agent as contributor, changelog for big product changes.
alwaysApply: true
---

1. Every commit message describes what changed and why. Title plus a short body. Match the repo style. Do not write "various fixes" or list files without saying what the user can now do.
2. Never add Co-authored-by Cursor, never name the agent as a contributor, and never set git author or committer to the agent.
3. If the change is big and user facing (new page, layout shift, product behavior people will notice), add a dated entry to `marketing/src/data/milestones.ts` whose title and summary match the commit, then include that file in the same commit. Skip the changelog for tiny copy tweaks and internal refactors.
4. Date changelog entries in the existing form, such as 17 AUG 2026. No em dash or en dash in that copy.
